column2:
Eurylochus, you indeed may stay here in this very place
272	eating and drinking beside the hollow black ship;
273	but I shall go, for strong necessity is upon me.

At your return, Zeus-nurtured, we are as glad
420	as if we had come to Ithaca, our fatherland;
421	but come, tell us of the destruction of the other comrades.

Zeus-born, this man we shall leave, if you bid,
444	to stay here by the ship and guard the ship;
445	but lead us to the sacred house of Circe.
